🚀 Feature
allow deepcopy on the jit module in the CPP frontend
Motivation
Let's say you have actor centric model which contains a mutable state buffer.
class ActorModel(jit.ScriptModule):
   def __init__(self):
       self.register_buffer("state", torch.tensor)

   def forward(self, x):
          // each forward mutates the internal buffer of this actor
          self.state += x
         // and then return some prediction
        return self.fancy_math(self.state, x)

You need to instantiate a new instance of said Actor Model for each new actor. This is trivial in python
inputs = [..., ...]
actors = [..., ...]
actor = ActorModel()
actors.append(actor)

for i, input in enumerate(inputs):
    actor(input)

However, if we use JIT, we cannot do this, because in the CPP frontend, the only way to instantiate a script module is by loading it
const auto actor = jit::load("actor.pt");

If we allow a deepcopy, I just need to load the torchscript graph once and do deepcopy for each new actor.
const auto actor_base = jit::load("actor.pt");
const auto new_actor = actor_base.deep_copy();
